.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command verifies certificate chains.
If a certificate chain has multiple problems, this program attempts to
display all of them.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Print out a usage message.
.It Sy -CRLfile Em filename Ns | Ns Em uri
The file or URI should contain one or more CRLs in PEM or DER format.
This option can be specified more than once to include CRLs from
multiple sources.
.It Sy -crl_download
Attempt to download CRL information for certificates via their CDP
entries.
.It Sy -show_chain
Display information about the certificate chain that has been built (if
successful).
Certificates in the chain that came from the untrusted list will be
flagged as "untrusted".
.It Sy -verbose
Print extra information about the operations being performed.
.It Sy -trusted Em filename Ns | Ns Em uri
A file or URI of (more or less) trusted certificates.
See
.Xr openssl-verification-options 1
for more information on trust settings.
.Pp
This option can be specified more than once to load certificates from
multiple sources.
.It Sy -untrusted Em filename Ns | Ns Em uri
A file or URI of untrusted certificates to use for chain building.
This option can be specified more than once to load certificates from
multiple sources.
.It Sy -vfyopt Em nm Ns : Ns Em v
Pass options to the signature algorithm during verify operations.
Names and values of these options are algorithm-specific.
.It Sy -nameopt Em option
This specifies how the subject or issuer names are displayed.
See
.Xr openssl-namedisplay-options 1
for details.
.It Sy -engine Em id
See
.Xr openssl 1 .
This option is deprecated.
.Pp
To load certificates or CRLs that require engine support, specify the
.Sy -engine
option before any of the
.Sy -trusted ,
.Sy -untrusted
or
.Sy -CRLfile
options.
.It Sy -CAfile Em file Ns , Sy -no-CAfile Ns , Sy -CApath Em dir Ns , Sy -no-CApath Ns , Sy -CAstore Em uri Ns , Sy -no-CAstore
See
.Xr openssl-verification-options 1
for details.
.It Sy -allow_proxy_certs Ns , Sy -attime Ns , Sy -no_check_time Ns , Sy -check_ss_sig Ns , Sy -crl_check Ns , Sy -crl_check_all Ns , Sy -explicit_policy Ns , Sy -extended_crl Ns , Sy -ignore_critical Ns , Sy -inhibit_any Ns , Sy -inhibit_map Ns , Sy -no_alt_chains Ns , Sy -partial_chain Ns , Sy -policy Ns , Sy -policy_check Ns , Sy -policy_print Ns , Sy -purpose Ns , Sy -suiteB_128 Ns , Sy -suiteB_128_only Ns , Sy -suiteB_192 Ns , Sy -trusted_first Ns , Sy -use_deltas Ns , Sy -auth_level Ns , Sy -verify_depth Ns , Sy -verify_email Ns , Sy -verify_hostname Ns , Sy -verify_ip Ns , Sy -verify_name Ns , Sy -x509_strict Sy -issuer_checks
Set various options of certificate chain verification.
See
.Xr openssl-verification-options 1
for details.
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
